<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>CodeBlog</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css" />
</head>

<body>

  <nav class="navbar">

    <h2 class="brand-name">CodeBlog</h2>

    <div class="profile-area">
      <span class="welcome-text">Welcome, <%= user %></span>

      <a href="/logout" class="logout-link">
        Logout
      </a>
    </div>

  </nav>


  <main class="page-content">

    <section class="hero-section">

      <span class="article-category">DEVELOPER JOURNEY</span>

      <h1 class="hero-title">
        Code. Create.
        <br />
        Keep Learning.
      </h1>

      <p class="hero-description">
        Welcome to my developer space where I share what I learn
        about web development, programming, backend technologies,
        projects and everything in between.
      </p>

    </section>


    <section class="articles-section">
      <article class="article-card">

        <span class="article-category">
          JAVASCRIPT
        </span>

        <h2 class="article-title">
          JavaScript Concepts Every Beginner Should Know
        </h2>

        <p class="article-description">
          Explore variables, functions, arrays, objects,
          promises and other important concepts that build
          a strong JavaScript foundation.
        </p>

        <a href="#" class="article-link">
          Explore article →
        </a>

      </article>
      <article class="article-card">

        <span class="article-category">
          REACT JS
        </span>

        <h2 class="article-title">
          Building Modern Interfaces With React
        </h2>

        <p class="article-description">
          Learn how components, props, state and hooks work
          together to create interactive and reusable
          React applications.
        </p>

        <a href="#" class="article-link">
          Explore article →
        </a>

      </article>
      <article class="article-card">

        <span class="article-category">
          BACKEND
        </span>

        <h2 class="article-title">
          Creating APIs With Node.js & Express
        </h2>

        <p class="article-description">
          Understand how backend applications work by
          creating REST APIs, handling requests and
          connecting applications with databases.
        </p>

        <a href="#" class="article-link">
          Explore article →
        </a>

      </article>
      <article class="article-card">

        <span class="article-category">
          DATABASE
        </span>

        <h2 class="article-title">
          Getting Started With MongoDB
        </h2>

        <p class="article-description">
          Learn about databases, collections, documents,
          CRUD operations and how MongoDB can store
          application data.
        </p>

        <a href="#" class="article-link">
          Explore article →
        </a>

      </article>
      <article class="article-card">

        <span class="article-category">
          PROJECTS
        </span>

        <h2 class="article-title">
          From Ideas to Real Projects
        </h2>

        <p class="article-description">
          Discover practical projects that combine
          frontend, backend and database technologies
          to solve real-world problems.
        </p>

        <a href="#" class="article-link">
          View projects →
        </a>

      </article>


      <!-- Learning -->
      <article class="article-card">

        <span class="article-category">
          LEARNING
        </span>

        <h2 class="article-title">
          Lessons From My Coding Journey
        </h2>

        <p class="article-description">
          Notes, mistakes, useful resources and experiences
          from continuously learning and building software
          as a developer.
        </p>

        <a href="#" class="article-link">
          Read more →
        </a>

      </article>


    </section>

  </main>

</body>

</html>